<newsitem itemid="104347" id="root" date="1996-10-09" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: NEW CENT RAISES HALF YR SHR, DIV.</title>
<headline>NEW CENT RAISES HALF YR SHR, DIV.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)	 </p>
<p>    Shr, headline (cts)	124.5   vs   105.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		    122.0   vs   105.0</p>
<p>    Total net earnings     2,199.0   vs 5,687.0</p>
<p>    Investment income	2,403.0   vs 2,085.0</p>
<p>    Net asset value (cts)  8,467.0   vs 6,746.0</p>
<p>Div payable: Dec 6</p>
<p>On register: Nov 1</p>
<p>Full name: New Central Witwatersrand Areas Ltd (mining</p>
<p>financial)</p>
<p>NOTE - Following the restructuring of Johannesburg</p>
<p>Consolidated Investment Co Ltd last year, the company</p>
<p>disposed of its investment in Johnnies Industrial Corp Ltd</p>
<p>and used the proceeds to increase its holding in Anglo</p>
<p>American Platinum Corp Ltd .</p>
<p>The company said that the surplus on realisation of</p>
<p>investments was thus not available for distribution.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
